Negative control for the record form's seeded model (RT4).

A form action whose manager publishes `{ schema, uischema, defaults }` and no
`model` — the affiliate withdrawal slot — takes its starting model from
`defaults`, so the drawer opens with the legacy prefilled message. This mutant
opens every such drawer on an empty model: the message field is blank, the
required-field gate holds Send disabled, and the prefilled sentence
(`text.affiliate_withdraw_balance`) is lost.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (component lane): record-surface.spec.ts — a form whose context
slot publishes `defaults` and no `model` must open on those defaults, and must
submit them untouched.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/RecordSurface.vue
@@ -834,7 +834,7 @@
     openRow.value = row;
     draft.value = action.form.prefill
       ? pick(row ?? model.value, keys(schemaOf(action.form)?.properties))
-      : cloneDeep(unref(slotOf(action.form)?.defaults) ?? {});
+      : {};
     openAction.value = action;
     return;
   }
